 "_doc": "How much the doer may do on its own. Tier A: read or trivially reversible -> just do it and report. Tier B: a reversible write (a setting, a note, a reminder on a site) -> do it, then report with a screenshot. Tier C: irreversible, outward, money or identity -> fill everything, screenshot the review page, STOP and post a checkpoint card; an owner's tap on the card runs the final step. Patterns are case-insensitive regexes; a hit on either list makes the step tier C. `never` is refused outright.",
